course: dictionary
lesson: 4394
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A haircut can mean two things. It can be the act of having your hair cut, as when you «get a haircut» at the barber. It can also mean the style or shape your hair is cut into, as in «a new haircut».
explain: Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits. In «You can choose your own clothes or haircut by discussing it with your parents», a haircut is a style you choose. In «a girl in Leeds told her friend her new haircut looked fine», it is the shape of her hair.
explain: Check with the swap test. Put "having my hair cut" or "the shape of my hair" into the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: Haircut is a noun: a haircut, haircuts.
fact: «Haircut» means the act of having your hair cut.
fact: «Haircut» can also mean the style or shape your hair is cut in.
fact: Useful phrases are «get a haircut», «need a haircut», «have a haircut» and «a new haircut».
fact: A hairdresser or barber gives you a haircut, and you may feel nervous or happy afterwards.
exercise: «I need a haircut before the school photo.» What does haircut mean here? | *The act of having your hair cut | A kind of shoe | The shape of a hat | A small cut on your finger
exercise: «She loved her new haircut, with short layers at the front.» What does haircut mean here? | Having a bath | *The style or shape her hair is cut in | A small hairy animal
exercise: Which phrase means you are going to have your hair cut? | *Get a haircut | Tie your laces | Blow your nose | Wash your hands
test: In «a girl in Leeds told her friend her new haircut looked fine», what is the haircut? | The act of paying for a trim | A pair of scissors | A hairy coat | *The style or shape of her hair
test: «You can choose your own clothes or haircut by discussing it with your parents.» What does haircut mean? | Feeling nervous at the barber | A tall building | *The style you pick for your hair | Lying down to rest
exam: What does haircut mean in «Famous people still buy chocolate, rewear dresses and get haircuts»? | A wet, grey day | A kind of old castle | *The act of having your hair cut | A cake with cream on top
